<%# The data card. It holds the table and nothing else.

    The page title and its actions used to live in a header strip inside this card.
    They belong at page level - see components/ui/_page_header, which every admin index
    page now renders above this. A title nested in the card reads as a section label
    rather than as the page's title, and left one surface doing two jobs. %>
<div class="tw-card">
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="table-base">
<%# The identifier column, which is the one that stays visible below lg. A caller can name it with
    `primary: true`; otherwise it is the first.

    The `id` fallback that used to sit here - skip the first column if it is an id - is gone with the id
    columns themselves. No index shows one now: an id is 62px of a 718px scroller at 1024px, and it is in the
    URL of the link in the same row. Keeping a branch for a shape nothing produces is how an unused rule
    starts looking like a supported one. %>
<% primary = columns.index { it[:primary] } || 0 %>

      <%# Below lg this table is **one column**: the identifier column's value, then every other as a
          labelled line, then the actions. Nine index tables render through here and each one scrolled
          sideways at 375px - 685px of overflow on admin/teachers, 632px on admin/users - carrying the
          data off the right edge of a scroll a phone user has to discover.

          Pinning the actions cell, which is what design.md previously called for, kept them reachable
          and kept the scroll. The reasoning was that three labelled ghosts are ~250px against a 343px
          viewport, so data and actions cannot share a row - true only while the actions have their own
          column. Collapsed into the primary cell they need no width of their own, and the scroll goes.
          The trading floor has done it this way since it was measured at left=370 in a 326px viewport,
          and it is the one table in the app that already fitted.

          This is Polaris's IndexTable condensed mode and Primer's guidance for the same problem. The
          headers go with their columns: a `<th>` for a column nobody can see names nothing. %>
      <thead>
        <tr class="table-header-row">
          <% columns.each_with_index do |column, index| %>
            <%# Column headers are chrome, not content: smaller and muted so they
                do not read at the same weight as the data. Matches tables.css. %>
            <th scope="col" class="table-header-cell table-header-cell-left <%= "hidden lg:table-cell" unless index == primary %>">
              <% if column[:sortable] %>
                <%= sort_link(column[:attribute], column[:label]) %>
              <% else %>
                <%= column[:label] %>
              <% end %>
            </th>
          <% end %>
          <% if options[:show_actions] != false %>
            <th scope="col" class="table-header-cell table-header-cell-right table-actions-cell hidden lg:table-cell">
              <span class="sr-only">Actions</span>
            </th>
          <% end %>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="bg-white">
        <% if collection.any? %>
          <% collection.each do |record| %>
            <tr class="table-body-row cursor-pointer" id="<%= dom_id(record) %>"
                data-controller="clickable-row"
                data-clickable-row-url-value="<%= url_for([:admin, route_model(record)]) %>"
                data-action="click->clickable-row#navigate">
              <% columns.each_with_index do |column, index| %>
                <%# The primary cell never gets `whitespace-nowrap`. Below lg it holds the whole row and
                    has to wrap; at lg it holds the prose - a name, a company, an email - and it is what
                    makes these tables wider than a Chromebook. Measured on admin/stocks at 1366px: 38px
                    of overflow with it, 0 without. The portfolio holdings table has always worked this
                    way, and design.md records that it "never scrolls at any width, because it adapts by
                    wrapping the company name".

                    The other cells keep it: a date breaking across two lines reads as a mistake, and a
                    figure is short. The testid stays on the real cell either way, so a test that reads a
                    column still reads that column. %>
                <td class="table-body-cell <%= "hidden whitespace-nowrap lg:table-cell" unless index == primary %>"
                    data-testid="<%= column[:attribute] %>">
                  <%# The primary column is always a link, not only when a caller remembers `link: true`.
                      The row navigates on click, and until this changed the only signifier of that was a
                      `cursor-pointer` that a duplicate `class` attribute had been swallowing - so the
                      record's own name looked like plain text on every admin index. `link: true` remains
                      for any *other* column that should point somewhere. %>
                  <% if index == primary || column[:link] %>
                    <%= link_to format_attribute(record, column[:attribute]), [:admin, route_model(record)], class: "tw-link" %>
                  <% else %>
                    <%= format_attribute(record, column[:attribute]) %>
                  <% end %>

                  <%# The rest of the row, below lg, in the one cell that is always on screen. %>
                  <% if index == primary %>
                    <% secondary = columns.each_with_index.reject { |_, i| i == primary } %>
                    <%= render "shared/stacked_row_fields",
                               fields: secondary.map { |c, _| [c[:label], format_attribute(record, c[:attribute])] },
                               actions: (if options[:show_actions] == false
                                           nil
                                         else
                                           render("admin/shared/table_row_actions", record: record)
                                         end) %>
                  <% end %>
                </td>
              <% end %>
              <% if options[:show_actions] != false %>
                <td class="table-body-cell table-body-cell-right hidden whitespace-nowrap table-actions-cell lg:table-cell">
                  <div class="flex items-center justify-end gap-1">
                    <%= render "admin/shared/table_row_actions", record: record %>
                  </div>
                </td>
              <% end %>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        <% else %>
          <%= render "admin/shared/empty_row",
                     colspan: columns.length + (options[:show_actions] == false ? 0 : 1),
                     title: options[:empty_title] || "Nothing here yet",
                     body: options[:empty_message],
                     action_label: options[:empty_action_label],
                     action_path: options[:empty_action_path] %>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <% if collection.respond_to?(:total_pages) && collection.total_pages > 1 %>
    <div class="px-4 py-3 border-t border-slate-200 lg:px-6">
      <%= render "admin/shared/pagination", collection: collection %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
